# Backend (`apps/api`)

NestJS, Better Auth (`@elynd/auth` + `@thallesp/nestjs-better-auth`), Drizzle (`@elynd/db`), Zod (`@elynd/shared`), Vitest.

Placement: **`layering`** + **`structure`**. Auth contracts: `.trellis/spec/api/backend/auth-monorepo.md` when touching auth. New domain feature: playbook **`create-api-feature`**.

## Naming

Nest **dot.role**: `auth.controller.ts`, `auth.service.ts`, `auth.module.ts` — not bare `route.ts` / `service.ts`.

## TypeScript

- Extend `../../tsconfig.base.json`; Nest-only flags stay in this app's `tsconfig.json`
- **Imports:** relative NodeNext with `.js` suffixes. No `@/` aliases until emit rewrite exists
- **DI:** constructor-injected classes/tokens = **value** imports; prefer `@Inject(Token)`. `import type` OK for pure types

## Layout

| Folder | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `src/modules/<domain>/` | Feature modules — create when first domain lands; do not pre-create empty `modules/` |
| `src/common/` | Pipes, filters, decorators — no domain workflows (flat) |
| `src/global/` | `global.module.ts` + global providers |
| `scripts/` | Offline TS (e.g. OpenAPI gen) via `pnpm exec tsx`; in `tsconfig.json`, excluded from `tsconfig.build.json` |

- Thin controllers: validate + map HTTP; rules in injectable services
- Auth in `@elynd/auth/server`; `AuthModule.forRoot` in `AppModule`; `load-env.ts` before auth import
- Prefer `@elynd/auth` types (`AuthUser` / `AuthSession`); no Adonis Access Token on Nest path
- Tech helpers never import feature modules

## Validation & OpenAPI

- Shared Zod helpers from `@elynd/shared/schemas` when applicable
- Feature HTTP DTOs from `@elynd/db` drizzle-zod in the feature module
- Project Zod pipe in `src/common`; OpenAPI via `openapi:gen` → `scripts/generate-openapi.ts` (`createOpenApiDocument`) for Apifox — no Swagger UI
- `@ApiProperty` needs explicit `type` under tsx (no `emitDecoratorMetadata`)
- Cross-app contracts → `@elynd/shared`, not duplicated in web

## Env

`DATABASE_URI`, `AUTH_SECRET`, `BETTER_AUTH_URL`, `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` via `@elynd/auth/env`.
